Package: qspquest
Type: Package
Title: Pharmacology Model Simulation and Bounded Estimation
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(person("Vivek", "Kohar", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "vivek.kohar@unibiointelligence.com"),
    person("UniBio Intelligence", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Compile pharmacokinetic, pharmacodynamic and quantitative systems
    pharmacology models with explicit physical units, then simulate dosing
    regimens, run parameter scans and Morris (1991)
    <doi:10.1080/00401706.1991.10484804> elementary-effects screens. Parameters
    are estimated within declared bounds by maximum likelihood or maximum a
    posteriori fitting for individual and pooled data, and by first-order
    conditional estimation with interaction (Wang 2007
    <doi:10.1007/s10928-007-9060-6>) or stochastic approximation
    expectation-maximization (Kuhn and Lavielle 2005
    <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2004.07.002>) for population data. Count and correlated
    binomial data can be fitted with Gamma-Poisson and probit-normal mixture
    models. A documented subset of 'NONMEM'-style dosing and observation records
    can be converted to model requests with source-row provenance. Computation
    uses the 'QSPQuest' engine, written in 'Rust', with stiff ordinary
    differential equation solvers from the 'diffsol' library.
